COMPILATION OF: E49I6

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49I6

   1 a 0000 E49I6:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P4] `rec.na >= rec.s2' -- the written-order twin of F4
   4 a 0006      at the same extents (3/2).  Expect `06 03 / 3E 02', JC da.
   5 a 0006      With I1..I5 this completes 4 relations x 2 orientations x
   6 a 0006      unequal extents; every row is compared against my arm-c
   7 a 0006      baseline bytes, which the primary hypothesis says are ALREADY
   8 a 0006      DR's bytes (NO arm). */
   9 c 0006   dcl
  10 c 0006     1 rec,
  11 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  12 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  13 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  14 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  15 c 0006   if rec.na >= rec.s2 then k = 1;
  16 c 001E   put list('K=', k);
  17 c 0040   stop;
  18 a 0043 end E49I6;

CODE SIZE = 0043
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
